    "confidence_notes": "High confidence extraction from VPW v1.1.3 AC/DC LUCI Premium VR script. Platform identified as SAM from LoadVPM call loading 'Sam.VBS'. ROM name 'acd_170h' from Const cGameName (color ROM variant 'acd_170hc' commented out). Trough is a 4-ball cvpmTrough with InitSwitches Array(21,20,19,18) — note reversed order means sw21 is nearest shooter, sw18 is nearest drain. Entry via Drain_Hit sub which calls bsTrough.AddBall. Trough eject (sol 1) fires bsTrough.ExitSol_On and also pulses sw22 (shooter lane confirm) when balls remain. Top eject (sol 12) uses cvpmSaucer at sw37 with PWM detection via SolModCallback — if PWM value reaches 255, an alternate high-power kickout fires (super skill shot mechanic). Bell eject (sol 52) is another cvpmSaucer at sw36. Lower PF eject (sol 3) is a 1-ball cvpmTrough at sw49. Impulse plunger at sw23 (sol 2). Cannon mechanism is complex: sw45 is the cannon kicker entry (Sw45_hit sets Controller.switch(45)=1), sw61/sw62 are cannon position switches set by animCannon based on GPos rotation (sw61=home at GPos>=110, sw62=mid-rotation at GPos<=89). Cannon motor is sol 32, cannon eject is sol 53. Bell swing uses a fake caged ball physics system — sw47 is the bell switch set True when bell RotX > 13 degrees. Band members mechanism on sol 51 uses repurposed Flipper1/Flipper2 objects for animation. Drop targets: AC/DC bank (sw1-5, sol 6 reset) and TNT bank (sw10-12, sol 7 reset) using DTHit/DTRaise framework. Flipper coils 15 (left) and 16 (right) use nFozzy with LF.Fire/RF.Fire and InitVpmFFlipsSAM. Mini playfield flippers on sol 4 (left) and sol 5 (right). Switches 86/88 are lower PF flipper button switches set via KeyDown/KeyUp (Controller.Switch(86)/88). Switch 64 is the FIRE button mapped to RightMagnaSave/LockbarKey. Switch 15 is tournament button (keyFront), switch 16 is start button. Lamps use Lampz framework with MassAssign — SAM platform uses lamp IDs from ChangedLamps. RGB LED inserts are driven by triplets of lamp IDs (e.g., lamp 81/82/83 = face mouth R/G/B). GI controlled via lamp IDs 130 (red), 132 (blue), 134 (lower PF), 136 (white). Flasher solenoids 17-31 use SolModCallback with SetLampMod mapping to lamp IDs 177-191, except sols 21/31 which use custom dome flasher subs (FlashSol121/FlashSol131). Sol 24 is knocker. Sol 8 is shaker motor. Sol 18 is detonator mechanism. Sol 54 is bell magnet. Sol 55 is cannon diverter. Sol 56 is right control gate via vpmSolGate. Sol 57 is left ramp diverter. Tilt uses vpmNudge.TiltSwitch = -7 (accelerometer-based, not a physical switch)."
  },
